<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antalya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Attalia, Adalia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antalya is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, on the Gulf of Antalya. Founded as Attalia by Attalus II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pergamon">Pergamon</a> in the 2nd century BCE, it became a Roman and Byzantine port and was captured by the Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> in 1207. Today it is a major port and one of Turkey's largest tourist centres.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antalya.jpg" alt="Antalya" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Esginmurat · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Falezlerden_Antalya_Konyaalt%C4%B1_Plaj%C4%B1na_do%C4%9Fru_bir_g%C3%B6r%C3%BCn%C3%BCm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
